<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Future Plans and Time Capsule</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How I Am Preparing for the Next Five Years</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Communication: Facilitate discussions on project goals and tasks. Text: Clarify written instructions in collaborative projects.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can facilitate a discussion on future goals for the time capsule using gestures (e.g., "What should we put in our time capsule?" while showing pictures of items like photos and letters.). Can clarify project instructions by listing steps on the board (e.g., "Step 1: Choose items; Step 2: Write descriptions."). Can help classmates understand project instructions by rephrasing in simple terms or using the native language when needed (e.g., "Everyone must bring a personal object for the project," while pointing to the list of items).</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays various images related to careers (e.g., engineer, doctor, software developer, artist) and future possibilities. Students brainstorm vocabulary previously learned related to future plans and career goals in pairs for 2 minutes. Then, the teacher asks, "What career might you pursue? What skills will you need?" encouraging the use of modals.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to clarify a simple instruction. "I will be working on a project about my future. The first step is to choose a career. 'Choose' means select or pick. For example, I choose to be a data analyst because I enjoy problem-solving." The teacher also models the pronunciation of /iː/ in words like "achieve" and "engineering" and stress in "critical thinking."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the first step in the project?" (Expected answer: Choose a career.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'pursue' mean in 'pursue a career'?" (Expected answer: To try to achieve/follow.)</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents the detailed written instructions for the "Career Planning Infographic" project on a slide or handout. The instructions outline steps like: "1. Research 2 high-demand careers you might pursue. 2. Outline required education and skills (e.g., leadership, critical thinking). 3. Describe an internship or community service opportunity you will be exploring. 4. Use modals and future continuous tense. 5. Include visuals."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> The ability to understand and interpret complex written project instructions and identify key requirements for a collaborative task. Focus on clarifying project steps and expectations.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Questions:</b> "What is the main goal of this project?" "What kind of information should your infographic include?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Students match phrases from the instructions (e.g., "high-demand careers," "future continuous tense") with their definitions or examples provided by the teacher, reinforcing vocabulary like "possibilities" and "opportunities."</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Mediation)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice mediating, clarifying, and rephrasing project instructions and personal career goals using modals for possibilities (e.g., "I might pursue..."), future continuous (e.g., "I will be working as..."), reported speech (e.g., "My teacher said that I should..."), and target vocabulary (career, goals, research, develop, leadership, critical thinking, internship).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Clarifying Instructions (Controlled Practice):</b> In pairs, students receive cards with project instructions written in more complex language. They must rephrase these instructions into simpler terms or using synonyms. For example, "The infographic should encapsulate your aspirations and pedagogical trajectory for the quinquennial span" becomes "Your infographic needs to show your goals and education plans for the next five years." They practice using reported speech: "The instructions said that we should explain our education plans."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Vocabulary Mediation (Semi-controlled Drill):</b> The teacher provides a list of key project vocabulary (e.g., "high-demand," "internship," "critical thinking," "community service"). In pairs, students take turns explaining these words to their partner, using gestures and rephrasing if needed, or even a brief explanation in their native language if communication completely breaks down (as per learning outcome). They focus on the pronunciation of stress in these multisyllabic words.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Goal Clarification (Pair Interaction):</b> Students interview each other about their potential career goals for the infographic, practicing asking peers about future goals for the time capsule (e.g., "What would you like to achieve in five years?"). They use modals ("I might consider medicine") and future continuous ("I will be studying biology") and practice explaining their choices, clarifying any ambiguities, and rephrasing if their partner doesn't understand.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Small group collaborative planning session for the "Career Planning Infographic." Students form groups of 3-4 and are tasked with outlining the main sections and content for *one* group infographic that reflects each member's career aspirations for the time capsule. Each group must assign a "Facilitator" and a "Clarifier."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The Facilitator (Sociolinguistic: organizes discussion, assigns roles) leads the discussion on what elements to include in their group's infographic based on the project instructions.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The Clarifier's (Mediation: helps classmates understand project instructions by rephrasing or using gestures) role is to ensure all group members fully understand each instruction and concept (e.g., "What does 'future-oriented' mean here?"). They use gestures (e.g., pointing to steps on the instruction sheet) and rephrasing to ensure shared understanding.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Group members share their individual career goals (using "I might pursue..." and "I will be working as...") and contribute ideas, explaining item choices (e.g., "I am including a picture of a robot because it represents my goal to become an electronic engineer in the future.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The group collaboratively decides on the content, ensuring the use of target grammar and vocabulary. The Clarifier helps summarize key decisions.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group briefly presents their preliminary infographic plan (2-3 minutes), focusing on how they clarified instructions, facilitated discussion, and reached a consensus on their collective goals. One group member (the Clarifier/Facilitator) explains one project instruction they had to clarify for their group and how they did it, using rephrased language. (e.g., "The instructions said we needed to mention 'education.' I clarified this by explaining it means 'what you learn at school or university' and gave examples like 'computer science' or 'medicine.'")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Observation Checklist/Peer Assessment):</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and intelligibility of explanation.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective use of target vocabulary (e.g., career, goals, education, skills, opportunities) and grammar (modals for possibilities, future continuous, reported speech).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Demonstrated ability to facilitate discussion and clarify project instructions (Mediation skill).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pronunciation of /iː/ sounds and appropriate word stress.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration and engagement in group activity.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of the infographic instructions did you find most challenging to understand or explain to your group, and how did you clarify it?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did you help your classmates understand their roles or tasks for the project?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"In what situations do you think mediation skills (like clarifying or rephrasing) are most useful in real life?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific mediation strategy did you use today that helped your group the most?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The class successfully practiced clarifying project instructions and facilitating discussions. The use of gestures and rephrasing was observed, aligning with the learning outcome. Some students still hesitated to use reported speech independently. Next time, more scaffolded opportunities for direct practice in rephrasing complex sentences could be beneficial. The project-based approach for mediation worked well to integrate all previous lessons.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson concludes the theme "How I Am Preparing for the Next Five Years" and the "Career Planning Infographic" project. The next lesson will introduce a new theme and set of learning objectives, building upon the collaborative and communicative skills developed in this unit.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">2 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>